{"text": "From: Katharina Vogelsang <k.vogelsang@vogelsang-stb.example>\nTo: Lorcan O Suilleabhain <lorcan@brightloom.example>\nCc: m.jansen@vogelsang-stb.example\nDate: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:51:33 +0200\nSubject: AW: Invoice 2026-0417 / VAT and bank details -- PLEASE READ before paying\n\nDear Lorcan,\n\nShort answers first, details below.\n\n1. Do NOT pay to the account in the PDF you received on Monday. That PDF did not come from us. Our bank details have not changed since 2019:\n\n   Account holder: Vogelsang Steuerberatung GmbH\n   Bank: Rheinufer Volksbank eG, Köln\n   IBAN: DE65 0954 8966 5692 8370 88\n   BIC: GENODED1RVK\n\n   The PDF shows an IBAN beginning NL75 -- that is not ours. Mareike has reported it to the police here (reference K-2026/331-4478). Please check whether anyone at Brightloom opened the attachment, and tell your IT people that the message came from IP 203.0.113.189 according to the header.\n\n2. VAT. Our invoice 2026-0417 for €3.850,00 is correctly issued WITHOUT German MwSt. You are a business customer in Ireland with a valid VAT number (IE3491226TH, I checked it in VIES this morning), so the reverse charge under Article 196 applies and you account for Irish VAT yourself. Our number, for your records: DE318847209.\n\n3. The Italian supplier. Atelier Conti S.r.l. charged you 22% Italian VAT on the sample fabrics (EUR 1.240,00 net). If the goods left Italy and you can prove transport to Kilkenny, that is wrong and Signor Conti should issue a credit note. If you collected the goods yourself at the fair in Milano, it is correct. Which was it?\n\nKind regards\nKatharina\n\nKatharina Vogelsang, Steuerberaterin\nVogelsang Steuerberatung GmbH | Agrippinaufer 41 | 50678 Köln\nTel. +49 221 5550 142 | Fax +49 221 5550 143\nAssistant: Mareike Jansen\n\n> -----Original message-----\n> From: Lorcan Ó Súilleabháin\n> Sent: Tuesday, 22 September 2026 17:14\n> To: Katharina Vogelsang\n> Subject: Invoice 2026-0417 / VAT and bank details\n>\n> Hi Katharina,\n>\n> Two things on your invoice for the German payroll registration.\n>\n> (a) Our bookkeeper says there should be 19% VAT on it and that without it Revenue\n> will query the deduction. Is she right? Brightloom Textiles Ltd. is registered here,\n> company no. 648213, if that matters.\n>\n> (b) We got an email yesterday saying you'd moved banks, with a new IBAN\n> (NL75 INGB 7240 6681 39). I was about to send the 3,850 euro from our\n> account (IE89AIBK69733626420599) but it looked off -- the sender was\n> k.vogelsang@vogelsang-stb.example.net, not your usual address. Can you confirm?\n>\n> Also, Fabrizio from Atelier Conti is chasing me for €1.512,80. I'd rather not pay\n> Italian VAT if I don't have to. I'm in Lyon at a fair until Friday -- mobile\n> +353 85 555 0147 is best.\n>\n> Thanks,\n> Lorcan\n> Finance Director, Brightloom", "kind": "Email", "detail": "461 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Katharina Vogelsang", "Lorcan O Suilleabhain", "Mareike Jansen", "Signor Conti", "Lorcan Ó Súilleabháin", "Fabrizio"], "companies": ["Vogelsang Steuerberatung GmbH", "Brightloom", "Vogelsang Steuerberatung", "Rheinufer Volksbank eG", "Atelier Conti S.r.l.", "Brightloom Textiles Ltd.", "Atelier Conti", "Vogelsang"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.6000000014901161, "modelMs": 25861.39999999851, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 25, "text": "Katharina Vogelsang", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Katharina Vogelsang"}, {"start": 27, "end": 60, "text": "k.vogelsang@vogelsang-stb.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "k.vogelsang@vogelsang-stb.example"}, {"start": 66, "end": 87, "text": "Lorcan O Suilleabhain", "kind": "person", "source": "mod